      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The new rule says SQLite decides emptiness, but the tokenizer shortcut treats `\\ufeff;` as nonempty even though SQLite skips it, so `\\ufeff; CREATE TABLE u(a,a,b); SELECT 1;` records the duplicate-column error twice. Fix: document this exception and qualify the one-event guarantee until boundary detection handles SQLite-skipped byte-order marks."
